// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
// Seawater Absorption — distance-based spectral attenuation for sound
// travelling through seawater. The underwater signature: lows survive for
// km, highs die within a km. See also README.md in the project repo.
//
// *** 2026-09-24: Spreading/Prop delay stayed at Sph/On (2026-09-23 memory-
// *** layout fix -- see the @init memory layout block + @serialize section --
// *** resolved the total-silence + T/S/depth/pH-snap bugs: unassigned array
// *** bases were all aliasing memory slot 0). Filter Engine reverted back to
// *** Fast: user reported much more attenuation than physics predicts (e.g.
// *** "very quiet at 4m", where Sph spreading alone should be only -12dB) on
// *** Accurate. That engine has never been confirmed correct against real
// *** REAPER playback -- its one unverified assumption from day one is
// *** whether fft_real/fft_permute pack bins the way stft_frame() assumes
// *** (see that function's comment). This symptom is consistent with gains
// *** landing on the wrong bins. Do not re-enable Accurate as default until
// *** that's actually confirmed correct by ear (transparent at 1m, no excess
// *** attenuation at short distances) -- Fast is the well-verified fallback.
// *** Separately, a still-open report exists of Distance being the only
// *** slider that "holds" during playback, with Model/Spreading/Wet/Prop
// *** delay/Filter Engine not holding -- this script's code never writes to
// *** sliders 2 or 7-12 at all (grep confirms only slider1 and slider3-6 are
// *** ever assigned), so that symptom, if still present, is not this
// *** plugin's logic. Check for a leftover automation envelope on those
// *** specific parameters (not just the automation mode selector), or test
// *** in a blank project to rule out project-state corruption.
//
// Install: copy into <REAPER resource>/Effects/ (or drag onto an FX chain), rescan FX browser.
// Recommended flow: Sound Particles output bus -> this plugin -> automate Distance to follow the scene source.
//
// --- Controls ---
//  World Preset    Sets Temperature/Salinity/Depth/pH to a real (or, for
//                  "Mesozoic AB", speculative) location in one click:
//                    N.Atl Ice   6.0C / 34.7ppt / 10m  / pH8.1  cold N. Atlantic surface, Iceland waters
//                    Arctic Ice -1.5C / 33.0ppt / 10m  / pH8.1  under polar ice, near-freezing
//                    SOFAR       3.6C / 35.0ppt / 1000m/ pH7.8  deep sound channel; sound travels enormous distances here
//                    Mediterr   19.0C / 38.2ppt / 50m  / pH8.1  warm and unusually salty
//                    Coastal    12.0C / 34.5ppt / 5m   / pH8.0  generic shallow coastal water
//                    Freshwater 18.0C / 0.1ppt  / 3m   / pH8.0  a lake -- salinity ~0 kills the MgSO4 absorption term
//                    Drumheller 21.0C / 0.35ppt / 3m   / pH8.2  Red Deer River, Drumheller AB, summer (real reference point)
//                    Mesozoic AB25.0C / 33.0ppt / 60m  / pH8.0  SPECULATIVE: Cretaceous Western Interior Seaway, ~80Mya
//                  Manually moving Temperature/Salinity/Depth/pH afterwards
//                  snaps this back to "User". Does NOT touch Distance, Model,
//                  Spreading, Extra dB, Wet, Prop delay, or Filter Engine --
//                  those are always yours to set independently.
//  Distance (m)    How far the sound has travelled underwater. Drives the
//                  absorption curve and, if enabled, Prop delay and Spreading.
//                  Default is 10m (deliberately close): absorption coloration
//                  and spreading loss operate on very different distance
//                  scales -- spreading is already -60dB by 1km while
//                  absorption is still subtle even at several km (see
//                  HANDOFF.md 2026-09-23 entry for the numbers). There is no
//                  single distance where both are dramatically audible at
//                  once; that's real physics, not a bug. 10m keeps the
//                  plugin listenable out of the box (spreading ~-20dB,
//                  absorption negligible, as it should be that close).
//                  Automate Distance up for real use -- it'll get darker AND
//                  much quieter together, which is the actual point. Swings
//                  to the 100km slider max: at 100km spherical spreading is
//                  ~-100dB and even mid-band absorption is crushing, so the
//                  output attenuates essentially to silence -- by design, so
//                  you can ride the full distance dial all the way down
//                  (a post gain/trim is the normal pairing). Add a
//                  gain/trim plugin after this one if you need to compensate
//                  loudness while riding Distance out to hundreds/thousands
//                  of meters.
//  Temperature/    Feed the speed-of-sound (Mackenzie) and, in Francois-
//  Salinity/Depth/ Garrison mode, the absorption curve itself. Salinity in
//  pH              particular controls the "MgSO4" absorption term -- this
//                  is why ocean water and a freshwater lake sound different.
//  Absorption      Thorp (1967): simple, fixed dB/km-vs-frequency curve,
//  model           ignores Temperature/Salinity/Depth/pH entirely, valid to
//                  ~50kHz. Francois-Garrison (1982, default): sums three
//                  physical loss mechanisms (boric acid = lows, magnesium
//                  sulfate = mids, pure water viscosity = highs) and
//                  actually responds to the sliders above -- more
//                  physically accurate, and the recommended default.
//  Spreading       Geometric spreading loss (sound spreading over an ever-
//                  bigger sphere/cylinder), separate from absorption --
//                  same effect in air or water. Sph (6dB/doubling, default)
//                  is the physically correct open-water case; Cyl (3dB/
//                  doubling) approximates a duct/channel; Off disables it
//                  (distance then only changes tone, not volume -- useful if
//                  an upstream tool, e.g. Sound Particles, already applies
//                  its own distance attenuation and you don't want it
//                  double-applied here).
//  Extra dB/       Manual attenuation added on top of Spreading, for
//  doubling        creative control beyond the physical model.
//  Wet (%)         Standard dry/processed blend.
//  Prop delay      Real propagation delay = Distance / speed-of-sound, so
//                  far sounds arrive later (like thunder trailing lightning).
//                  On by default; turn off if an upstream tool already
//                  applies its own arrival-time delay.
//  Filter Engine   Fast (5-band, default): the absorption curve applied as
//                  gains across a 5-way crossover (300/1k/3k/9k) -- cheap,
//                  audibly correct, and the only engine confirmed correct
//                  in live REAPER so far. Accurate (FFT): 2048-pt STFT
//                  applies the exact curve per ~23Hz bin instead of 4
//                  crossover points, in principle more accurate, but its
//                  fft_real/fft_permute bin-packing has never been
//                  confirmed correct live -- a 2026-09-24 report of much
//                  more attenuation than physics predicts is consistent
//                  with gains landing on the wrong bins. Try it, but treat
//                  it as unverified until confirmed transparent at 1m with
//                  no excess loss at short distances. ~43ms extra latency
//                  when active (reported to the
//                  host via pdc_delay, auto-compensated in REAPER).
//
// --- Physics (verified against sources, see HANDOFF.md) ---
//  Speed of sound : Mackenzie (1981)         valid 2-30C, 25-40ppt, 0-8000m
//  Absorption     : Francois-Garrison (1982)  valid ~10-500kHz, -2..22C, 30-35ppt, 0-3.5km (R `sonar` pkg / NPL guide / NOAA paper)
//                  boric-acid A1 uses 8.86/c (NOT 8.686/c) per F&G 1982 + Ainslie-McColm cross-check
//  Fallback       : Thorp (1967) extended,    dB/km, valid < ~50 kHz, independent of T/S/depth
//
// --- Filter engines ---
// Fast: each crossover stage is a 4th-order complementary pair (LP =
// Butterworth-2 x 2, HP forced to '1 - LP') so the band sum telescopes to
// unity with zero droop.
// Accurate: STFT overlap-add, 512-sample hop (75% overlap), Hann window;
// per-bin gain 10^(-alpha(f_bin)*dist_km/20). See HANDOFF.md for the
// verification story (and one important caveat: Hann^2 @ 75% overlap sums
// to 1.5, not 1 -- both this file's window and the Python reference divide
// by sqrt(1.5) to correct for it).
//
// Relevant reference implementation: Epi_Doppler
//   https://github.com/ThanasisEpitideios/Epi_Doppler  (distance delay + smoothed params in JSFX)
// Behaviour reference (air medium): TDR Proximity (local copy in "scope and context/proximity_v1_0_1-mac reference")

desc:Seawater Absorption
options:maxmem=64000000

slider1:preset=0<0,8,1{User,N.Atl Ice,Arctic Ice,SOFAR,Mediterr,Coastal,Freshwater,Drumheller,Mesozoic AB}>World Preset
slider2:sea_dist=10<1,100000,1>Distance (m)
slider3:sea_temp=10<-2,30,0.1>Temperature (C)
slider4:sea_sal=35<0,40,0.1>Salinity (ppt)
slider5:sea_depth=10<0,8000,1>Depth (m)
slider6:sea_ph=8.0<7.5,8.5,0.01>pH
slider7:sea_model=1<0,1,1{Thorp,Francois-G}>Absorption model
slider8:sea_spread=6<0,6,1{Off,,,Cyl (3dB),,,Sph (6dB)}>Spreading
slider9:sea_atten=0<-18,18,0.5>Extra dB/doubling
slider10:sea_mix=100<0,100,1>Wet (%)
slider11:sea_delay=1<0,1,1{Off,On}>Prop delay
slider12:sea_engine=0<0,1,1{Fast (5-band),Accurate (FFT)}>Filter Engine

@init
// All functions are defined first, as the very first thing inside @init,
// so every call site (including init_xover() further down in this same
// section) resolves. Two things learned live, the hard way:
//  1. REAPER's JSFX compiler does NOT forward-reference a function defined
//     later in the same section -- it must be defined above its first use.
//  2. Code placed *before* the first @section header (@init/@slider/@sample)
//     is NOT compiled at all -- REAPER silently drops it. (Tried putting the
//     functions there first; got the identical 'init_xover' undefined error,
//     which is what revealed this.) Functions must live inside a section.

// speed of sound (Mackenzie 1981), m/s
// Note: written as plain decimals, not 5.304e-2-style scientific notation --
// REAPER's JSFX/EEL2 compiler does not accept that literal syntax (confirmed
// live: 'syntax error' right at the 'e-2' in 5.304e-2).
function sea_mack(t, s, z) (
  1448.96 + 4.591*t - 0.05304*t*t + 0.0002374*t^3
    + 1.340*(s-35) + 0.01630*z + 0.0000001675*z*z
    - 0.01025*t*(s-35) - 0.0000000000007139*t*z^3
);

// absorption in dB/km, f in kHz, t/s/z/ph/c = temp/salinity/depth/pH/speed-of-sound
//  model 0 = Thorp (extended), model 1 = Francois-Garrison
// Takes t/s/z/ph/c explicitly (rather than reading sea_temp/etc. globals)
// so the FFT engine can evaluate it against its own smoothed parameters
// without disturbing the fast-path globals.
function sea_alpha(f, t, s, z, ph, c) local(a1a, f1a, a2a, p2a, f2a, a3a, p3a) global(sea_model) (
  sea_model == 0 ?
    ( 0.11*f*f/(1+f*f) + 44*f*f/(4100+f*f) + 0.000275*f*f + 0.003 )
  : (
    // boric acid (dominates lows)  A1 per F&G 1982 = 8.86/c
    a1a = (8.86/c) * (10^(0.78*ph - 5));
    f1a = 2.8*sqrt(max(s,0.001)/35) * (10^(4 - 1245/(t+273)));

    // magnesium sulfate (mids)
    a2a = 21.44*(s/c)*(1 + 0.025*t);
    p2a = 1 - 0.000137*z + 0.0000000062*z*z;
    f2a = (8.17*(10^(8 - 1990/(t+273)))) / (1 + 0.0018*(s-35));

    // pure water viscosity (highs)
    a3a = (t <= 20) ?
        (0.0004937 - 0.0000259*t + 0.000000911*t*t - 0.000000015*t^3)
      : (0.0003964 - 0.00001146*t + 0.000000145*t*t - 0.00000000065*t^3);
    p3a = 1 - 0.0000383*z + 0.00000000049*z*z;

    a1a*f1a*f*f/(f1a*f1a + f*f) + a2a*p2a*f2a*f*f/(f2a*f2a + f*f) + a3a*p3a*f*f
  )
);

// ---- crossover: 4th-order complementary pairs (LP + HP == 1 exactly) ----
// stages at 300/1k/3k/9k: LP = 2 cascaded Butterworth 2nd-order sections (4th
// order); HP is forced to the exact z-complement '1 - LP' so the multi-stage
// band sum telescopes to unity with zero droop (verified vs impulse test).
function set_stage4(idx, fc) local(w0, cw, sw, al, n, bs0, bs1, bs2, as1, as2, n0, n1, n2, n3, n4, d1, d2, d3, d4) global(fb0, fb1, fb2, fb3, fb4, fa1, fa2, fa3, fa4, srate) (
  w0 = 2 * $pi * fc / srate;
  cw = cos(w0); sw = sin(w0);
  al = sw * 0.707106781186548;
  n = 1 + al;
  bs0 = (1-cw)*0.5/n; bs1 = (1-cw)/n; bs2 = (1-cw)*0.5/n;
  as1 = (-2*cw)/n;    as2 = (1-al)/n;
  // 4th order: N = B*B (LP numerator), D = A*A (denominator)
  n0 = bs0*bs0;            n1 = 2*bs0*bs1;
  n2 = bs1*bs1 + 2*bs0*bs2;
  n3 = 2*bs1*bs2;          n4 = bs2*bs2;
  d1 = 2*as1;              d2 = as1*as1 + 2*as2;
  d3 = 2*as1*as2;          d4 = as2*as2;
  // lowpass
  fb0[idx] = n0; fb1[idx] = n1; fb2[idx] = n2; fb3[idx] = n3; fb4[idx] = n4;
  fa1[idx] = d1; fa2[idx] = d2; fa3[idx] = d3; fa4[idx] = d4;
  // highpass = (D - N)/D
  fb0[idx+1] = 1 - n0; fb1[idx+1] = d1 - n1; fb2[idx+1] = d2 - n2; fb3[idx+1] = d3 - n3; fb4[idx+1] = d4 - n4;
  fa1[idx+1] = d1; fa2[idx+1] = d2; fa3[idx+1] = d3; fa4[idx+1] = d4
);

function init_xover() (
  set_stage4(0, 300);
  set_stage4(2, 1000);
  set_stage4(4, 3000);
  set_stage4(6, 9000);
  // right channel gets its own filter state (idx+8) so L/R don't share history
  set_stage4(8, 300);
  set_stage4(10, 1000);
  set_stage4(12, 3000);
  set_stage4(14, 9000)
);

// one 4th-order DF1 section
function sec4(idx, x) local(y) global(fb0, fb1, fb2, fb3, fb4, fa1, fa2, fa3, fa4, xs1, xs2, xs3, xs4, ys1, ys2, ys3, ys4) (
  y = fb0[idx]*x + fb1[idx]*xs1[idx] + fb2[idx]*xs2[idx] + fb3[idx]*xs3[idx] + fb4[idx]*xs4[idx]
      - fa1[idx]*ys1[idx] - fa2[idx]*ys2[idx] - fa3[idx]*ys3[idx] - fa4[idx]*ys4[idx];
  xs4[idx] = xs3[idx]; xs3[idx] = xs2[idx]; xs2[idx] = xs1[idx]; xs1[idx] = x;
  ys4[idx] = ys3[idx]; ys3[idx] = ys2[idx]; ys2[idx] = ys1[idx]; ys1[idx] = y;
  y
);

// ---- STFT overlap-add filter: window -> fft_real -> per-bin gain -> ifft_real -> window ----
// inb/outb are buffer base offsets (inbufL/outbufL or inbufR/outbufR), so this
// runs once per channel per hop. `wp` marks the newest sample in the ring;
// wp+1 (wrapped) is the oldest, i.e. the chronological start of the frame.
// fft_real/ifft_real packing per REAPER JSFX docs: size real in -> size/2
// complex out, first pair is (DC, Nyquist), rest are (real,imag) bin pairs;
// normally paired with fft_permute/fft_ipermute; no automatic 1/size scaling.
function stft_frame(inb, outb) local(i, k, g, idx) global(wp, FFTN, half, winbuf, scblk, gainb) (
  idx = wp + 1; (idx >= FFTN) ? idx -= FFTN;
  i = 0;
  while (i < FFTN) (
    scblk[i] = inb[idx] * winbuf[i];
    idx += 1; (idx >= FFTN) ? idx -= FFTN;
    i += 1;
  );
  fft_real(scblk, FFTN);
  fft_permute(scblk, half);
  scblk[0] *= gainb[0];        // DC
  scblk[1] *= gainb[half];     // Nyquist
  k = 1;
  while (k < half) (
    g = gainb[k];
    scblk[2*k]   *= g;
    scblk[2*k+1] *= g;
    k += 1;
  );
  fft_ipermute(scblk, half);
  ifft_real(scblk, FFTN);
  idx = wp + 1; (idx >= FFTN) ? idx -= FFTN;
  i = 0;
  while (i < FFTN) (
    outb[idx] += (scblk[i] / FFTN) * winbuf[i];
    idx += 1; (idx >= FFTN) ? idx -= FFTN;
    i += 1;
  );
);

// ---- memory layout & buffer bases -----------------------------------
// REAPER JSFX memory is a single buffer indexed in *items* (4-byte floats,
// default pool ~8M items; see advfunc.php). Root cause of the 2026-09-23
// no-output + slider-snap bug: none of the array bases were ever assigned.
// fb0..fb4/fa1..fa4/xs1..xs4/ys1..ys4 and dlbL/dlbR all sat at 0, winbuf was
// 0, so every "array" aliased slot 0 and the crossover memsets + init_xover()
// + delay memset + Hann-window build clobbered each other; sec4() then
// solved y = prev_y * x -> output collapsed to ~zero.
// All bases are now distinct, non-overlapping, and assigned before any use.
// Layout (items):
//   crossover  17 x 16-stride arrays   65536 .. 65807
//   STFT       win/in/out/scblk/gain    131072 .. ~144384
//   delay      L=196608, R=196608+dlsize  (dlsize = 75*srate)
// scblk (and the FFT's working span) stays fully inside the 65536-item
// block [131072, 196608), so it never crosses a 65,536-item boundary
// (fft_real/ifft_real requirement, advfunc.php).
FFTN = 2048; HOP = 512; half = FFTN/2;
dlsize = srate * 75;             // ~75s buffer: physical prop delay up to the
                                 // 100km slider max (100km / 1400 m/s = 71s);
                                 // needs options:maxmem above (8M default too small at >48k).

fb0 = 65536; fb1 = 65552; fb2 = 65568; fb3 = 65584; fb4 = 65600;
fa1 = 65616; fa2 = 65632; fa3 = 65648; fa4 = 65664;
xs1 = 65680; xs2 = 65696; xs3 = 65712; xs4 = 65728;
ys1 = 65744; ys2 = 65760; ys3 = 65776; ys4 = 65792;
winbuf  = 131072;
inbufL  = winbuf  + FFTN;
outbufL = inbufL  + FFTN;
inbufR  = outbufL + FFTN;
outbufR = inbufR  + FFTN;
scblk   = outbufR + FFTN;
gainb   = scblk   + FFTN;
dlbL = 196608;
dlbR = dlbL + dlsize;

// ---- fast-path crossover filter design ----
memset(fb0, 0, 16); memset(fb1, 0, 16); memset(fb2, 0, 16); memset(fb3, 0, 16); memset(fb4, 0, 16);
memset(fa1, 0, 16); memset(fa2, 0, 16); memset(fa3, 0, 16); memset(fa4, 0, 16);
memset(xs1, 0, 16); memset(xs2, 0, 16); memset(xs3, 0, 16); memset(xs4, 0, 16);
memset(ys1, 0, 16); memset(ys2, 0, 16); memset(ys3, 0, 16); memset(ys4, 0, 16);
init_xover();
memset(dlbL, 0, dlsize); memset(dlbR, 0, dlsize);

// ---- accurate-path STFT engine (2048/512, 75% overlap, causal single-ring-
// buffer OLA -- see seawater_absorption.py StftEngine, verified there to
// <0.05dB freq-response error and exact-sample reconstruction/latency) ----
memset(inbufL, 0, FFTN); memset(outbufL, 0, FFTN);
memset(inbufR, 0, FFTN); memset(outbufR, 0, FFTN);
memset(gainb, 0, half + 1);
freembuf(dlbR + dlsize);
// Hann window, pre-scaled by 1/sqrt(1.5) so analysis+synthesis (applied
// twice) overlap-added at 75% reconstructs exact unity gain -- Hann^2 @
// 75% overlap sums to 1.5, not 1; confirmed numerically (1.11e-15 spread)
// in the Python reference. Do not drop this factor.
wi = 0;
while (wi < FFTN) (
  winbuf[wi] = (0.5 - 0.5*cos(2*$pi*wi/FFTN)) / sqrt(1.5);
  wi += 1;
);
wp = 0; hcount = 0;
sm_temp = slider3; sm_sal = slider4; sm_depth = slider5; sm_ph = slider6;
sm_distkm = max(slider2, 1) / 1000;

// ---- state ----
dlw = 0;
dl_cur = 0;
last_pres = preset;              // don't re-apply the startup preset
last_temp = slider3; last_sal = slider4; last_depth = slider5; last_ph = slider6;

gs0 = 1; gs1 = 1; gs2 = 1; gs3 = 1; gs4 = 1;
gsv = 1;

@slider
// ---- world presets (move the T/S/depth/pH sliders) ----
preset != last_pres ? (
  last_pres = preset;
  preset == 1 ? ( slider3 = 6.0;  slider4 = 34.7; slider5 = 10;    slider6 = 8.1; );  // N. Atlantic surface (Iceland waters)
  preset == 2 ? ( slider3 = -1.5; slider4 = 33.0; slider5 = 10;    slider6 = 8.1; );  // Arctic under-ice
  preset == 3 ? ( slider3 = 3.6;  slider4 = 35.0; slider5 = 1000;  slider6 = 7.8; );  // deep SOFAR channel
  preset == 4 ? ( slider3 = 19.0; slider4 = 38.2; slider5 = 50;    slider6 = 8.1; );  // Mediterranean
  preset == 5 ? ( slider3 = 12.0; slider4 = 34.5; slider5 = 5;     slider6 = 8.0; );  // coastal shallow
  preset == 6 ? ( slider3 = 18.0; slider4 = 0.1;  slider5 = 3;     slider6 = 8.0; );  // freshwater lake
  preset == 7 ? ( slider3 = 21.0; slider4 = 0.35; slider5 = 3;     slider6 = 8.2; );  // Red Deer River, Drumheller AB, summer
  preset == 8 ? ( slider3 = 25.0; slider4 = 33.0; slider5 = 60;    slider6 = 8.0; );  // Cretaceous Western Interior Seaway (Mesozoic AB, speculative)
  last_temp = slider3; last_sal = slider4; last_depth = slider5; last_ph = slider6;
) : (
  // a manual tweak of T/S/depth/pH invalidates the preset -> snap dropdown to "User"
  // Epsilon compare, not != : exact float equality is unsafe here -- values
  // like 34.7/8.1 aren't exactly binary-representable, and if REAPER
  // re-asserts a slider's value through its own rounding during playback
  // (can happen every block, not just on real user changes), a 1-ULP
  // mismatch against our own last-set value would read as "manually
  // changed" and reset the preset to User on every single block. Confirmed
  // live: this was resetting to baseline continuously during playback.
  (abs(slider3-last_temp) > 0.0001 || abs(slider4-last_sal) > 0.0001 || abs(slider5-last_depth) > 0.0001 || abs(slider6-last_ph) > 0.0001) ? (
    preset != 0 ? ( preset = 0; slider1 = 0; slider_automate(slider1); last_pres = 0; );
    last_temp = slider3; last_sal = slider4; last_depth = slider5; last_ph = slider6;
  );
);
sea_temp = slider3;
sea_sal = slider4;
sea_depth = slider5;
sea_ph = slider6;
sea_engine = slider12;

sea_c = sea_mack(sea_temp, sea_sal, sea_depth);
dist_km = max(sea_dist, 1) / 1000;

// per-band absorption gains (band-centre freqs in kHz)
g0 = 10^(-sea_alpha(0.20, sea_temp, sea_sal, sea_depth, sea_ph, sea_c)*dist_km/20);
g1 = 10^(-sea_alpha(0.55, sea_temp, sea_sal, sea_depth, sea_ph, sea_c)*dist_km/20);
g2 = 10^(-sea_alpha(1.70, sea_temp, sea_sal, sea_depth, sea_ph, sea_c)*dist_km/20);
g3 = 10^(-sea_alpha(5.20, sea_temp, sea_sal, sea_depth, sea_ph, sea_c)*dist_km/20);
g4 = 10^(-sea_alpha(15.0, sea_temp, sea_sal, sea_depth, sea_ph, sea_c)*dist_km/20);

// broadband: geometric spreading (6 or 3 dB/doubling) + manual dB/doubling
(sea_dist > 1) ? ( sea_db = (sea_spread + sea_atten) * log(sea_dist)/log(2); ) : ( sea_db = 0; );
sea_db < 0 ? sea_db = 0;
glv = 10^(-sea_db/20);

// propagation delay ~ distance / c, smoothed in @sample
dlt = (sea_dist/sea_c) * srate;
(dlt > dlsize - 2) ? dlt = dlsize - 2;
(dlt < 0) ? dlt = 0;

mix = sea_mix/100;
delay_on = (sea_delay == 1);

// one-pole smoothing coefficients (~30ms / ~60ms time constants)
gk = 1 - exp(-1/(0.03*srate));
dlk = 1 - exp(-1/(0.06*srate));

@sample
pdc_delay = (sea_engine == 1) ? FFTN : 0;    // report STFT latency for delay compensation

gsv += (glv - gsv) * gk;

sea_engine == 1 ? (
  // ---- accurate path: STFT overlap-add, exact per-bin absorption ----
  // smooth the underlying scalars (not the gain curve itself -- the curve
  // is only recomputed once per hop, ~10.7ms @48k, which is already smooth
  // enough given these move at Distance-automation rates, not per-sample)
  sm_distkm += (dist_km - sm_distkm) * gk;
  sm_temp   += (sea_temp  - sm_temp)  * gk;
  sm_sal    += (sea_sal   - sm_sal)   * gk;
  sm_depth  += (sea_depth - sm_depth) * gk;
  sm_ph     += (sea_ph    - sm_ph)    * gk;

  inbufL[wp] = spl0;
  inbufR[wp] = spl1;
  wetL = outbufL[wp]; outbufL[wp] = 0;
  wetR = outbufR[wp]; outbufR[wp] = 0;

  hcount += 1;
  (hcount >= HOP) ? (
    hcount = 0;
    smc = sea_mack(sm_temp, sm_sal, sm_depth);
    k = 0;
    while (k <= half) (
      fkhz = (k * srate / FFTN) * 0.001;
      gainb[k] = 10^(-sea_alpha(fkhz, sm_temp, sm_sal, sm_depth, sm_ph, smc) * sm_distkm / 20);
      k += 1;
    );
    stft_frame(inbufL, outbufL);
    stft_frame(inbufR, outbufR);
  );

  wp += 1; (wp >= FFTN) ? wp = 0;
) : (
  // ---- fast path: smoothed 5-band gains to avoid zipper on automation ----
  gs0 += (g0 - gs0) * gk;
  gs1 += (g1 - gs1) * gk;
  gs2 += (g2 - gs2) * gk;
  gs3 += (g3 - gs3) * gk;
  gs4 += (g4 - gs4) * gk;

  // 5-band crossover, left
  b0 = sec4(0, spl0);  hp0 = sec4(1, spl0);   // band1 (LP@300) / stage B in (HP@300)
  b1 = sec4(2, hp0);   hp1 = sec4(3, hp0);    // band2 (300..1k) / stage C in
  b2 = sec4(4, hp1);   hp2 = sec4(5, hp1);    // band3 (1k..3k) / stage D in
  b3 = sec4(6, hp2);   hp3 = sec4(7, hp2);    // band4 (3k..9k) / band5 (HP@9k)
  wetL = gs0*b0 + gs1*b1 + gs2*b2 + gs3*b3 + gs4*hp3;

  // same, right (separate filter state at idx 8..15)
  b0 = sec4(8, spl1);  hp0 = sec4(9, spl1);
  b1 = sec4(10, hp0);  hp1 = sec4(11, hp0);
  b2 = sec4(12, hp1);  hp2 = sec4(13, hp1);
  b3 = sec4(14, hp2);  hp3 = sec4(15, hp2);
  wetR = gs0*b0 + gs1*b1 + gs2*b2 + gs3*b3 + gs4*hp3;
);

// ---- propagation delay (smoothed, linear-interpolated circular buffer) ----
(delay_on) ? (
  dlw += 1;
  (dlw >= dlsize) ? dlw = 0;
  dlbL[dlw] = wetL;
  dlbR[dlw] = wetR;
  dl_cur += (dlt - dl_cur) * dlk;
  rp = dlw - dl_cur;
  (rp < 0) ? rp += dlsize;
  (rp >= dlsize) ? rp -= dlsize;
  i0 = floor(rp);
  fr = rp - i0;
  i1 = i0 + 1;
  (i1 >= dlsize) ? i1 = 0;
  dL = dlbL[i0] + (dlbL[i1] - dlbL[i0]) * fr;
  dR = dlbR[i0] + (dlbR[i1] - dlbR[i0]) * fr;
) : (
  dL = wetL;
  dR = wetR;
);

// broadband spreading gain + wet/dry
spl0 = spl0*(1-mix) + dL*gsv*mix;
spl1 = spl1*(1-mix) + dR*gsv*mix;

@serialize
// Deliberately trivial -- its mere presence is the fix: a non-empty
// @serialize section tells REAPER NOT to re-zero memory/variables before
// @init, and @init re-runs on playback start and samplerate change (js.php).
// Without this, last_pres/last_temp/last_sal/last_depth/last_ph were wiped
// each time playback started, so the preset-apply / manual-tweak detection
// in @slider fired spuriously and snapped sliders back to file defaults
// (2026-09-23 slider-snap bug). Keep this section non-empty.
nop = 0;